From \cite{Goldberg2013OnTM}, we know that given  a nonzero $N\in \mca N_n$, 
{the matrix $P\in \mca P_n$ that maximizes the angle between $N$ and $\mca P_n$} 
is the negative semidefinite part of $N$, that is, if $N = Q\Lambda Q^\top$ is the eigendecomposition of $N$, then $P =Q\Lambda^-Q^\top = Q(Q^\top NQ)^-Q^\top$.
